## 1. Project Overview

The Retail Sales and Inventory Optimization project implements an end-to-end data engineering and analytics solution using Azure Databricks.

The solution integrates retail sales transactions, inventory movements, sales returns and master data into a centralized Lakehouse architecture.

It transforms raw operational data into trusted business datasets and provides analytical capabilities through Databricks AI/BI Dashboards, Genie and MLflow.

The primary business objectives are:
- Improve retail sales visibility.
- Maintain reliable inventory movement records.
- Support sales-return analysis.
- Reconcile stock balances and business metrics.
- Enable interactive business intelligence.
- Introduce AI-assisted analytics and demand forecasting.

